<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Wuzhang Plains</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">234</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Wuzhang Plains was a stand-off in 234 between the Shu Han army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhuge-liang">Zhuge Liang</a> and the Wei forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sima-yi">Sima Yi</a>, on the Wei river in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. It was Zhuge Liang's fifth and last northern expedition. Sima Yi refused to give battle, and after months of stalemate Zhuge Liang fell ill and died in camp, and the Shu army withdrew.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-wuzhang-plains.jpg" alt="Battle of Wuzhang Plains" width="320" height="260" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Living_Zongda_Fleeing.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
